This prints something like `work took 8.208µs`, not about 100 ms. Why? Give the one-line fix.
```go
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"time"
)

func work() {
	start := time.Now()
	defer fmt.Println("work took", time.Since(start))
	time.Sleep(100 * time.Millisecond)
}

func main() {
	work()
}
```

What does this print, and why do the two results differ?
```go
package main

import "fmt"

func f() (n int) {
	defer func() { n *= 2 }()
	return 3
}

func g() int {
	n := 3
	defer func() { n *= 2 }()
	return n
}

func main() {
	fmt.Println("f() =", f())
	fmt.Println("g() =", g())
}
```
